## Conventions and completeness

All variables are real unless the problem specifies natural numbers. [t] means floor(t), the greatest integer not exceeding t; {t}=t-floor(t), with 0 <= {t} < 1. Negative integer parts are not truncations toward zero. These standard conventions are stated explicitly because this exercise-only lesson contains zero definition paragraphs.

Natural-number indexing in 707 is taken as n=1,2,...; an n=0 convention is also handled below. An ordinary nonzero geometric progression has a nonzero ratio. No unprinted positivity restriction is silently imposed on an integer-indexed progression.

Coverage: 43 consecutive exercises 682-724, all 127 printed/Latin-mapped labeled parts, and every task inside unlabeled exercises. Compound parts 689, 709 and 711 retain all requested comparisons or quantities. Graph requests are covered by concrete construction instructions, coordinates, shapes, crossings and boundary inclusions, not by numeric answers alone.

The graph descriptions below are complete reproducible constructions, not claims that an unprovided historical 698/699 plot was viewed. No new image payload or original-1978 graph/table equivalence is invented.

